6:/// Generic atomic type for GPU-only shared memory operations.
7:///
8:/// Atomic<T> is a compiler-known marker type used to declare atomic buffers:
9:/// `Array<Atomic<u32>, N>` or `Array<Atomic<i32>, N>`. It is NOT a value type and
10:/// MUST NOT be used in CPU-side code. Atomic elements are accessed via
11:/// `atomic_add(buf, idx, val)`, `atomic_sub`, `atomic_max`, etc. inside GPU kernels.
12:///
13:/// T must be one of: u32, i32. No f32, f64, i64, or other types are supported.
14:/// (WGSL atomics are integer-only; no hardware float atomics are portable.)
15:///
16:/// This type is a compiler built-in; no methods are defined on it.
17:/// The struct has no user-accessible fields (compiler-only marker).
